## Point to Convey to Professor
- [] tcp-sequence will not unique always but the probability of collision is very low, as it is picked random for a connection.
to get the same tcp seq, OS has to Reuse the exact same ephemeral port and also Randomly pick the exact same sequence number out of a 4.29 billion number range. also When that HTTP request finishes and the connection closes, Linux puts port 45092 into a state called TIME_WAIT for 60 seconds so if we choose the batch of less than that then we wont have much issue.